-- title:
--   Integrality of Y^{2M}j^{M+1}(j-1728)^M over ℂ[1/j]
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \ge 1$ and a finite-index subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ containing the principal congruence subgroup $\Gamma(M)$, and assume that $1$ lies in the strict periods of the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$. Let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for that image, and write $\hat{f} \in \mathbb{C}((q))$ for the Laurent series attached to its $q$-expansion `qExpansion 1` of width $1$. Let $\hat\jmath =$ `coeffEmb ℂ jq` be the image in $\mathbb{C}((q))$, under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$, of the Laurent series `jq` $= q^{-1} \cdot$ `jNumQ` over $\mathbb{Q}$, where `jNumQ` is the rational power series obtained from the integral power series `jNum`. Let $Y \in \mathbb{C}((q))$ satisfy $Y \cdot \theta(\hat\jmath) = \hat{f}$, where $\theta =$ `thetaL ℂ` is the $\mathbb{C}$-linear operator $q\,d/dq$ on $\mathbb{C}((q))$, i.e. multiplication by $q$ composed with the Laurent-series derivative. The conclusion is that the element $$Y^{2M} \, \hat\jmath^{\,M+1} \, (\hat\jmath - 1728)^M$$ of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ is integral over the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by $\hat\jmath^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the integrality step in the $q$-expansion analysis of weight-two cusp forms on a level containing $\Gamma(M)$: classically the displayed element is $G/E_4^M$ with $G = f^{2M}E_4^3/\Delta$ a modular form of weight $4M$ on $\Gamma$, holomorphic at the cusps because every cusp width divides $M$, and integrality over $\mathbb{C}[1/j]$ comes from taking the norm down to level one. It is used to derive the lower bound on the order of vanishing in [`ModularCurve.one_sub_ord_le_ord_of_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_eq_qExpansion_of_gamma_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.one_sub_ord_le_ord_of_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_eq_qExpansion_of_gamma_le).
